# Docs hub and Pillar A/B update guardrails

## Canonical places to edit

| Kind of content | Edit here |
|-----------------|-----------|
| Hub pages, pipeline write-ups, vendor teaching pages, navigation | `docs/` |
| Motadata Pillar A and Pillar B contracts, discussion notes, labs for that work | `pillar-ab-implementation/` |
| Management PDFs and OKR workbooks | `KR Plan/` (do not duplicate under `docs/`) |

The HTTP docs hub is served from `benchmarking/dashboard/` on port 8765. That folder should only **link** to the canonical files above. Never maintain a separate evolving copy of the same markdown or HTML there.

## Writing while documenting

Follow the project rule on plain, complete writing:

- Prefer full, definite sentences over short slogans.
- Do not invent option letters or private path names for decisions.
- Define any necessary short name in ordinary language the first time it appears on the page.
- Restate locks and boundaries so a reader without chat history can act.

## After you change structure or titles

1. Update `docs/NAVIGATION.md` when a page moves or a new primary surface appears.
2. Keep Motadata kickoff and the Pillar A/B slice reachable from the hub (implementation slice at repo-root `pillar-ab-implementation/`).
3. Leave teaching annexes discoverable from the HLD archive page rather than crowding the main menu.
4. Smoke-check important hub URLs on port 8765 when you change links or mounts.
